+
+## Sign-up phone verification
+
+Sign-up sends and checks six-digit SMS codes through [Twilio Verify](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api). Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID` in the server environment (see `.env.example`). Configure the Verify service for six-digit codes and enable service rate limits for production, especially across multiple instances. Without credentials, the form reports that verification is unavailable; it never simulates delivery or accepts a test code.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint sends codes, verifies them, and registers users with the existing registration service. An expiring, signed, HTTP-only cookie gates registration after verification. The existing external registration service remains responsible for account persistence and its own access controls; this repository cannot enforce verification on clients calling that external service directly. The verified phone is forwarded as `phone`; persisting it requires support in that external service.
+
+The form supports a single labeled code input, keyboard entry, pasting, `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, and progressive WebOTP extraction on supported secure origins. For WebOTP, configure the SMS template to end with an origin-bound line such as `@your-domain.example #123456`, using the actual code and hostname. See [WebOTP's SMS format](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebOTP_API). Manual entry remains available on all devices. Codes expire according to the Verify service's policy; the form supports resending after 30 seconds.
